CONTROLS|tool=ymcheck|source=cmd/ymcheck/main.go|source_sha256=d899f019d23e966d0457ed3e6596fe4d633ad7b2a58142f78afd52f3408c7373|go=go1.24.7|json=0
# Every command runs in work/ (relative to this file) with ../checker = ymcheck and ../ymgen = generator/reference.
# 'fail' means: exit status 2 and stdout exactly one line FAIL|reason=<prefix>...|json=0, with no CERT and no STORE row.
# 'pass' means: exit status 0, CERT row(s) and one STORE row with merkle=PASS, row_sums_zero=PASS, w_symmetry=PASS.
# Layout (owner's payload-only decision): header 4096 bytes + payload_bytes; rows first, then zero bytes up to
# payload_bytes (inside the merkle); bytes after payload_bytes are room-file bytes, read and counted, never interpreted.
# Controls marked [CHANGED ...], [EXTENDED ...], [renamed ...] or [NEW] are the ones that decision changed; section E is new.

CONTROL|id=A01|verdict=MATCH|json=0
  name:     go vet
  command:  go vet ./...
  expected: exit 0
  actual:   exit=0
  stdout:   

